/* Valid: P holds at every non-negative x (its greatest fixpoint is x >= 0),
   so x = 121 is a witness.  Every witness lies beyond 120, so an elimination
   of the existential that searches for a witness in [-100, 100] only finds
   none, and the problem it leaves behind is refutable although this one is
   not: that refutation must not be printed as invalid. */
exists (x: int). x > 120 /\ P x
s.t.
P (x: int): bool =nu x >= 0 /\ P (x + 1);
